WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.212
Random numbers are extremely useful for simulation, testing, and statistical experiments.

00:00:06.212 --> 00:00:13.427
Modern NumPy recommends creating a random-number generator with N P dot random dot default RNG.

00:00:13.427 --> 00:00:15.077
In this example, we use a seed of forty-two.

00:00:15.077 --> 00:00:21.882
The seed is important because it makes the generated sequence reproducible.

00:00:21.882 --> 00:00:27.517
If you run the same code with the same seed, you should receive the same simulated values.

00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:35.197
We generate eight observations from a normal distribution centered around one hundred with a standard

00:00:35.197 --> 00:00:39.197
deviation of fifteen. Click Run and inspect the sample and its mean.

00:00:39.197 --> 00:00:46.362
A different seed will produce a different sample, while the same seed helps another analyst reproduce your

00:00:46.362 --> 00:00:48.537
result. This is a professional habit.

00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:55.782
When randomness is part of an analysis, documenting the seed can make experiments, examples,

00:00:55.782 --> 00:00:57.615
and debugging much easier to reproduce.
